{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NJ6Xb1iAo1CiXZewmtiHUx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Book-KCNA commission — design and execution record\n3\tstatus: approved by the author 2026-08-23; executing\n4\tauthor: the author + Claude collaboration\n5\tdate: 2026-08-23\n6\trelates_to:\n7\t  - pipeline/config.yaml (book key `kcna`)\n8\t  - pipeline/book_orchestrator.py (B1–B6)\n9\t  - pipeline/orchestrator.py (14-stage chapter pipeline)\n10\t  - ../certcomp-diagrams (figure pass)\n11\t  - knowledge-base/voice/style-decisions.md (role families, seniority, subject dignity)\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t# Book-KCNA commission\n15\t\n16\t## 1. What is being built\n17\t\n18\tA Lodestar Ledgers study guide for the **Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA)** — CNCF / Linux Foundation's entry-level, multiple-choice cloud native credential. Repo `rookdarrow/Book-KCNA`, local `../Book-KCNA`, pipeline key `kcna`.\n19\t\n20\t## 2. Exam facts (verified 2026-08-23)\n21\t\n22\t| Fact | Value | Source |\n23\t|---|---|---|\n24\t| Price | $250 exam-only ($299 with LFS250; $495 with THRIVE-ONE) | training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-cloud-native-associate |\n25\t| Format | Online, proctored, multiple choice | same |\n26\t| Duration | 90 minutes | same |\n27\t| Attempts / eligibility / validity | Two attempts included · 12-month eligibility · valid 2 years | same |\n28\t| Prerequisites | None | same |\n29\t| Question count / passing score | 60 questions / 75% — widely cited, **not stated on the LF page**; the book labels them as such | third-party (sailor.sh, devopscube) |\n30\t| Curriculum | Restructured **effective no earlier than 2025-11-24**; observability folded into Cloud Native Architecture | training.linuxfoundation.org/kcna-program-changes |\n31\t\n32\tDomains and competencies (CNCF `KCNA_Curriculum.pdf`, current):\n33\t\n34\t| Domain | Weight | Competencies |\n35\t|---|---|---|\n36\t| Kubernetes Fundamentals | 44% | Kubernetes Core Concepts · Administration · Scheduling · Containerization |\n37\t| Container Orchestration | 28% | Networking · Security · Troubleshooting · Storage |\n38\t| Cloud Native Application Delivery | 16% | Application Delivery · Debugging |\n39\t| Cloud Native Architecture | 12% | Observability · Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles · Cloud Native Community and Collaboration |\n40\t\n41\tMost competing study material still teaches the retired five-domain blueprint (46/22/16/8/8 with a separate Observability domain). This book targets the current one.\n42\t\n43\t## 3. Decisions (ratified with the author 2026-08-23)\n44\t\n45\t- **Gates:** the author delegated every gate (book-outline final, per-chapter revision and integration) to the Claude session running the commission. The session reads each artifact before approving and records material concerns in this file.\n46\t- **Role family / tier:** The Communications Officer, **junior** tier — the associate rung beneath CKA's senior comms officer; peer tier to Network+ (cross-vendor peers share a tier per style-decisions [LOCKED 2026-04-19]). Voice stays the unified brand voice; only atmospheric register and reader positioning differ.\n47\t- **Figures:** full diagram pass through `certcomp-diagrams` after drafting (render, visual review, `--apply`).\n48\t- **Naming:** pipeline-native `chapter-NN-slug.md`, `00-front-matter.md`, `00-table-of-contents.md`, `kcna-glossary.md`, `the-lodestar.md` (Proxmox pattern), so no retrofit scripts are needed.\n49\t- **Relationship to Book-CKA:** conceptual, multiple-choice orientation — mental models and discrimination between plausible alternatives, not kubectl drills. CKA is cross-referenced as the next voyage; no chapter text is copied between the books.\n50\t- **Second checkout:** `../Books/KCNA` is a plain clone kept in sync by push/pull (author's convention, as for CKA).\n51\t\n52\t## 4. Execution plan\n53\t\n54\t1. **Scaffold** — repo with README + .gitignore, published; `kcna` registered in `certcomp/pipeline/config.yaml` and `certcomp-diagrams/config.yaml`.\n55\t2. **Sources** — authoritative snapshots cached in `Book-KCNA/sources/` with the research-stage frontmatter (LF exam page + change notice, CNCF curriculum, kubernetes.io concept docs per competency, CNCF cloud native definition and project maturity levels, Kubernetes community/SIG structure, OpenTelemetry + Prometheus overviews, OpenGitOps principles, Helm, OCI, twelve-factor). Per-chapter Stage 2 research adds chapter-specific snapshots later.\n56\t3. **Book outline** — `book_orchestrator.py --book kcna --run` through B1–B5; session reviews `arc-outline.md` against the domain weights, question budget (≥300 floor; 60-question mock), and prerequisite ordering before approving.\n57\t4. **Chapters** — `orchestrator.py --book kcna --run --chapter N` for every chapter, run in the background, gates approved after the session reads the draft; Proxmox metrics predict ~95 min wall per chapter.\n58\t5. **Book-level artifacts** — `reconcile.py --write` (TOC + drift report), B6 `the-lodestar.md`, `00-front-matter.md`, `kcna-glossary.md`, README status; structural lint to 0 fails.\n59\t6. **Diagram pass** — Stage 10 `image-specs.md` → sources → render → visual review → `--apply`; lint again.\n60\t7. **Push** after each milestone; pull `Books/KCNA`.\n61\t\n62\t## 5. Open items / risks\n63\t\n64\t- Long unattended pipeline runs on the Max subscription may hit usage limits; the orchestrator's per-stage state allows resuming.\n65\t- Question count / passing score are not on the LF page; front matter must hedge (\"commonly reported\").\n66\t- Voice-2 stage failed 8 times during the Proxmox run (retries succeeded); watch for the same.\n67\t\n68\t## 6. Gate log\n69\t\n70\t- **2026-08-23 — book_outline_final: approved (delegated to session).** 20 chapters (orientation · 17 content · synthesis · mock), Parts II–V map one-to-one onto the four domains, weight arithmetic 44/28/16/12 exact. Notes: B3 (retrieval architecture) called `Write` instead of emitting to stdout, so only its summary survived; B5 carried B3's stated figures forward and marked six reconstructed themes `[B5-reconstructed]` — accepted; rerun B3 only if a future reconcile needs the full schedule. B5 deliberately keeps D4.3 (community & collaboration) inside Ch 17 with its own sections and three checkpoints rather than a 21st chapter — accepted. B4 wrapped its body in a fence — cosmetic. Fixed the cp1252 `✓` banner bug in both orchestrators before starting chapters (it was re-running completed LLM stages).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e31eebcc-5cdf-41f6-9a4d-ad3448ff2836","uuid":"71614a4d-e784-403c-9545-36e5d30b9344","timestamp":"2026-08-24T03:41:52.550Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\certcomp\\HANDOFF_KCNA_COMMISSION.md","content":"---\ntitle: Book-KCNA commission — design and execution record\nstatus: approved by the author 2026-08-23; executing\nauthor: the author + Claude collaboration\ndate: 2026-08-23\nrelates_to:\n  - pipeline/config.yaml (book key `kcna`)\n  - pipeline/book_orchestrator.py (B1–B6)\n  - pipeline/orchestrator.py (14-stage chapter pipeline)\n  - ../certcomp-diagrams (figure pass)\n  - knowledge-base/voice/style-decisions.md (role families, seniority, subject dignity)\n---\n\n# Book-KCNA commission\n\n## 1. What is being built\n\nA Lodestar Ledgers study guide for the **Kubernetes and Cloud Native Associate (KCNA)** — CNCF / Linux Foundation's entry-level, multiple-choice cloud native credential. Repo `rookdarrow/Book-KCNA`, local `../Book-KCNA`, pipeline key `kcna`.\n\n## 2. Exam facts (verified 2026-08-23)\n\n| Fact | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Price | $250 exam-only ($299 with LFS250; $495 with THRIVE-ONE) | training.linuxfoundation.org/certification/kubernetes-cloud-native-associate |\n| Format | Online, proctored, multiple choice | same |\n| Duration | 90 minutes | same |\n| Attempts / eligibility / validity | Two attempts included · 12-month eligibility · valid 2 years | same |\n| Prerequisites | None | same |\n| Question count / passing score | 60 questions / 75% — widely cited, **not stated on the LF page**; the book labels them as such | third-party (sailor.sh, devopscube) |\n| Curriculum | Restructured **effective no earlier than 2025-11-24**; observability folded into Cloud Native Architecture | training.linuxfoundation.org/kcna-program-changes |\n\nDomains and competencies (CNCF `KCNA_Curriculum.pdf`, current):\n\n| Domain | Weight | Competencies |\n|---|---|---|\n| Kubernetes Fundamentals | 44% | Kubernetes Core Concepts · Administration · Scheduling · Containerization |\n| Container Orchestration | 28% | Networking · Security · Troubleshooting · Storage |\n| Cloud Native Application Delivery | 16% | Application Delivery · Debugging |\n| Cloud Native Architecture | 12% | Observability · Cloud Native Ecosystem and Principles · Cloud Native Community and Collaboration |\n\nMost competing study material still teaches the retired five-domain blueprint (46/22/16/8/8 with a separate Observability domain). This book targets the current one.\n\n## 3. Decisions (ratified with the author 2026-08-23)\n\n- **Gates:** the author delegated every gate (book-outline final, per-chapter revision and integration) to the Claude session running the commission. The session reads each artifact before approving and records material concerns in this file.\n- **Role family / tier:** The Communications Officer, **junior** tier — the associate rung beneath CKA's senior comms officer; peer tier to Network+ (cross-vendor peers share a tier per style-decisions [LOCKED 2026-04-19]). Voice stays the unified brand voice; only atmospheric register and reader positioning differ.\n- **Figures:** full diagram pass through `certcomp-diagrams` after drafting (render, visual review, `--apply`).\n- **Naming:** pipeline-native `chapter-NN-slug.md`, `00-front-matter.md`, `00-table-of-contents.md`, `kcna-glossary.md`, `the-lodestar.md` (Proxmox pattern), so no retrofit scripts are needed.\n- **Relationship to Book-CKA:** conceptual, multiple-choice orientation — mental models and discrimination between plausible alternatives, not kubectl drills. CKA is cross-referenced as the next voyage; no chapter text is copied between the books.\n- **Second checkout:** `../Books/KCNA` is a plain clone kept in sync by push/pull (author's convention, as for CKA).\n\n## 4. Execution plan\n\n1. **Scaffold** — repo with README + .gitignore, published; `kcna` registered in `certcomp/pipeline/config.yaml` and `certcomp-diagrams/config.yaml`.\n2. **Sources** — authoritative snapshots cached in `Book-KCNA/sources/` with the research-stage frontmatter (LF exam page + change notice, CNCF curriculum, kubernetes.io concept docs per competency, CNCF cloud native definition and project maturity levels, Kubernetes community/SIG structure, OpenTelemetry + Prometheus overviews, OpenGitOps principles, Helm, OCI, twelve-factor). Per-chapter Stage 2 research adds chapter-specific snapshots later.\n3. **Book outline** — `book_orchestrator.py --book kcna --run` through B1–B5; session reviews `arc-outline.md` against the domain weights, question budget (≥300 floor; 60-question mock), and prerequisite ordering before approving.\n4. **Chapters** — `orchestrator.py --book kcna --run --chapter N` for every chapter, run in the background, gates approved after the session reads the draft; Proxmox metrics predict ~95 min wall per chapter.\n5. **Book-level artifacts** — `reconcile.py --write` (TOC + drift report), B6 `the-lodestar.md`, `00-front-matter.md`, `kcna-glossary.md`, README status; structural lint to 0 fails.\n6. **Diagram pass** — Stage 10 `image-specs.md` → sources → render → visual review → `--apply`; lint again.\n7. **Push** after each milestone; pull `Books/KCNA`.\n\n## 5. Open items / risks\n\n- Long unattended pipeline runs on the Max subscription may hit usage limits; the orchestrator's per-stage state allows resuming.\n- Question count / passing score are not on the LF page; front matter must hedge (\"commonly reported\").\n- Voice-2 stage failed 8 times during the Proxmox run (retries succeeded); watch for the same.\n\n## 6. Gate log\n\n- **2026-08-23 — book_outline_final: approved (delegated to session).** 20 chapters (orientation · 17 content · synthesis · mock), Parts II–V map one-to-one onto the four domains, weight arithmetic 44/28/16/12 exact. Notes: B3 (retrieval architecture) called `Write` instead of emitting to stdout, so only its summary survived; B5 carried B3's stated figures forward and marked six reconstructed themes `[B5-reconstructed]` — accepted; rerun B3 only if a future reconcile needs the full schedule. B5 deliberately keeps D4.3 (community & collaboration) inside Ch 17 with its own sections and three checkpoints rather than a 21st chapter — accepted. B4 wrapped its body in a fence — cosmetic. Fixed the cp1252 `✓` banner bug in both orchestrators before starting chapters (it was re-running completed LLM stages).\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
